1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,240
A cruise ship is a building
that floats, and the thing that tells

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:04,540
you a building is in trouble

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:05,440
is the floor.

4
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,940
On a January night off the Italian

5
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:11,660
coast, four thousand two
hundred and twenty-nine

6
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:15,860
people felt a floor stop being level. It took
sixty-nine minutes to give the order to leave.

7
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,200
The people who investigated it worked

8
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,989
out that everybody could have got off.

9
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,753
So what used up the sixty-nine minutes?

10
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:25,750
Start with the weather,

11
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,780
because it removes an excuse before anyone

12
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:28,680
can reach for it.

13
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:30,280
The sea and the weather

14
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,701
that night were favourable.

15
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,140
No storm.

16
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:34,220
No fog.

17
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,500
No wind.

18
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,020
Whatever happened here, the weather

19
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:38,920
did not do it.

20
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,260
It is the thirteenth

21
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:41,540
of January, 2012.

22
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,240
The Costa Concordia is on a weekly

23
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:47,200
Mediterranean cruise, working her way round

24
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,200
a circuit of ports,

25
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,540
picking people up and setting them down

26
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:51,440
as she goes.

27
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,680
There are four thousand two hundred

28
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:58,385
and twenty-nine people on board. Three
thousand two hundred and six passengers.

29
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:00,710
One thousand and twenty-three crew.

30
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,063
Hold that second number.

31
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:04,703
A thousand crew is not a skeleton staff.

32
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:06,640
It is a workforce the size

33
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:07,540
of a factory.

34
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:10,060
Now the number that decides this film.

35
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,520
Of the three thousand two hundred

36
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:16,827
and six passengers, one thousand two
hundred and seventy had attended a muster.

37
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:18,098
A muster is the drill.

38
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:20,190
You put on the orange jacket,

39
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:21,240
walk to a marked point

40
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:22,300
on a specific deck,

41
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,831
and stand there while somebody counts you.

42
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,780
It exists so that on the worst

43
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:28,740
night, your legs already know

44
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:29,640
where to go.

45
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:31,944
One thousand two hundred and seventy

46
00:01:31,949 --> 00:01:32,858
had done it.

47
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:37,114
Those were the people who had joined the ship
at Savona, at the start of the circuit.

48
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:43,000
Everyone else received their safety instructions
by video. Four hundred and sixty-three

49
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:43,947
of them at Toulon.

50
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:46,650
Four hundred and fifty-six at Barcelona.

51
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,260
More at the ports after that.

52
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:49,998
That is not a scandal,

53
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,004
and it matters to say why first.

54
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,420
A ship on a circuit takes passengers

55
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:55,360
on at every stop.

56
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:57,940
You cannot run a full muster daily

57
00:01:57,940 --> 00:02:00,180
for a few hundred arrivals without emptying

58
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:01,601
the decks of everyone else,

59
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,260
and the rules of the time allowed

60
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,660
the briefing another way.

61
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,668
The arrangement was legal,

62
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:09,098
ordinary, and used by the whole industry.

63
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:13,580
It also meant that on the night
this happened, nearly two thousand people

64
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:15,200
on that ship had never once walked

65
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,463
to their muster station.

66
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:18,160
The ship is running south

67
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,160
of Giglio Island.

68
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,720
At four minutes and five seconds past

69
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,100
nine forty-four, she is three tenths

70
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,620
of a mile from a set

71
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,594
of rocks called Le Scole,

72
00:02:27,607 --> 00:02:28,670
making sixteen knots.

73
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:32,320
And she is half a mile south-west
of her planned route - much closer

74
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,004
to the coast than the plan says.

75
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:35,580
Half a mile.

76
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:38,016
On a chart, a finger's width.

77
00:02:38,017 --> 00:02:39,940
On the water, at sixteen knots,

78
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:40,887
under two minutes.

79
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:43,960
At seven seconds past nine forty-five,

80
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:46,800
the hull strikes the rock furthest east

81
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:50,978
of Le Scole, on the left side. Fifty-one seconds
later, the recorder captures the blackout.

82
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:55,710
The rudder and the bilge pumps lose
power. Seven seconds after that,

83
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,372
the emergency generator starts.

84
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,219
It runs for forty-one seconds.

85
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:01,520
Then it stops being able to supply

86
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,597
the ship's essential services continuously

87
00:03:03,627 --> 00:03:06,040
- and the two essential services named

88
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,600
in the report are the rudder

89
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:08,600
and the bilge pump.

90
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,394
The rudder is how you steer.

91
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:11,860
The bilge pump is how

92
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:12,807
you get water out.

93
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,740
Both of them, gone, inside
a minute and a half.

94
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,680
The master gives rudder
orders at forty-three

95
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:21,551
and forty-six seconds past nine forty-six.

96
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,800
The report states plainly that those orders

97
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,400
would have had no effect even

98
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,558
if they were executed.

99
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:29,060
There is nothing to execute them with.

100
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:31,120
And that is not bad luck.

101
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:32,700
It is geometry.

102
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,260
A ship this size is divided across

103
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,365
its length into watertight compartments,

104
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:40,036
and the machinery is distributed among them.

105
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:44,207
Compartment five held the propulsion electric
motors, and the fire and bilge pumps.

106
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:46,040
Compartment six held three

107
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,619
of the main diesel generators.

108
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:49,849
Those are the two the rock opened.

109
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:53,207
The pumps and the generators
were in the compartments that filled.

110
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:56,860
So the water came in through the hole,
and the two things

111
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:59,470
that could have fought the water -

112
00:03:59,471 --> 00:04:01,244
the power and the pumping -

113
00:04:01,245 --> 00:04:02,666
were standing in the water.

114
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:03,920
The size of the hole

115
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:05,236
was not known that night.

116
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:06,700
It was worked

117
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,911
out in the days afterwards.

118
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,700
Fifty-three metres.

119
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:13,800
Longer than the wingspan of an airliner,
opened along the side of the hull

120
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,700
in a few seconds.

121
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:17,920
Go back to the drill,

122
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,780
because everything that follows

123
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:20,900
runs through it.

124
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,200
A muster station

125
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,463
is not a safety theatre.

126
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:26,929
It is a piece of engineering
that happens to be made of people.

127
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,585
Here is what it does.

128
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,120
It takes several thousand strangers spread

129
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:33,600
across fifteen decks, and converts them

130
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:35,820
into countable groups
standing in known places,

131
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:36,880
next to the boats.

132
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,080
That conversion takes time.

133
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:40,963
That is the point of it.

134
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,720
You do the walking in advance,

135
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,480
in daylight, so that the walking

136
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,440
is already done

137
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,651
when the lights go out.

138
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,080
And a ship the size

139
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:49,720
of this one has muster stations

140
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:52,180
that the investigators describe as capacious

141
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:54,060
and suitable - big enough,

142
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,903
and in the right places.

143
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:57,946
The infrastructure was there.

144
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,920
The rehearsal, for most
of the people aboard, was not.

145
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,740
Now put the two facts

146
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:03,687
beside each other.

147
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,120
Nearly two thousand passengers

148
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,020
had watched a video.

149
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,400
And the ship had lost all electrical

150
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,020
power to its essential systems

151
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:12,300
inside ninety seconds.

152
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:16,420
What happens to a video briefing
in a corridor with no lights in it?

153
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,183
The report answers this,

154
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,640
and its answer is the bluntest passage

155
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,798
in the whole document.

156
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:25,651
Passengers were not directed to muster
stations according to procedure.

157
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:27,680
There was chaos and confusion,

158
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,154
and a lack of communication.

159
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:31,420
In the report's own words:

160
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:34,480
a complete disorganisation, mainly

161
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,954
because nobody on the bridge
coordinated the emergency.

162
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,260
That sentence names the failure precisely,

163
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:41,200
and notice where it puts it.

164
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:42,798
Not on the passengers.

165
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:44,626
Not on the crew on the decks.

166
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:45,893
On the coordination.

167
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,700
Because the same paragraph
contains the other

168
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:50,640
half, and any film that leaves

169
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:51,740
this out is not telling

170
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:52,640
you the truth.

171
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,616
Passengers testified that despite the chaos,

172
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:59,980
and despite how little they had been prepared,
crew members supported them

173
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,875
with humanity and effective action -

174
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:06,600
and ferried them to the boats and off the ship.
A thousand crew, most of them

175
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,758
with no instruction coming from anywhere,

176
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:10,540
improvised an evacuation.

177
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:15,620
And the people they carried off said
so afterwards, on the record, to investigators.

178
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,220
That is not the story this accident

179
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:19,580
is usually told as.

180
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:23,240
Two hundred and seventy-two of that thousand

181
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:26,460
had joined the ship since the first
of December. A quarter of the workforce,

182
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:27,960
turned over in six weeks.

183
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,840
Twelve of them had embarked that same day.

184
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:34,218
And the investigators looked hard
at that, and then set it aside.

185
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,440
The turnover was almost entirely

186
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,387
in the hotel and service departments.

187
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:40,464
Very few key personnel were new.

188
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:45,540
The Body's conclusion is that the replacements
are to be considered irrelevant to how

189
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:46,540
the crew performed.

190
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:48,620
That finding is worth respecting,

191
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:51,000
because it closes off an easy answer.

192
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:53,028
This was not a green crew.

193
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:55,771
The Body's own assessment is the opposite.

194
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:57,420
Taken as a whole,

195
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:00,280
it says, the crew gave an adequate

196
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,180
performance in the core phase

197
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:05,240
of the evacuation - moving passengers

198
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,600
off the ship until about four

199
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,580
in the morning, with the vessel listed

200
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:11,580
at eighty degrees,
in conditions it describes

201
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:12,540
as very dangerous.

202
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:14,473
Four in the morning.

203
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:15,915
At eighty degrees.

204
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:18,025
So if the people were not the problem,

205
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,032
look at what was reaching them.

206
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:23,840
There is a rule that the company
operating a ship must establish a language

207
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,460
of work, so that safety

208
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:26,776
performance is effective.

209
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,440
Somebody wrote that rule because somebody,

210
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:31,660
once, could not be understood.

211
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:33,320
The crew of this ship

212
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,688
were of thirty-eight
different nationalities.

213
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:38,501
The passengers came
from twenty-six countries.

214
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:40,372
The company had chosen Italian.

215
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:42,140
The Body is careful here,

216
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,740
and its care is the point.

217
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,920
Formally, it says, the choice

218
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:48,011
is not open to censure -

219
00:07:48,012 --> 00:07:51,205
the ship was Italian-flagged
and the paperwork had to be in Italian.

220
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,240
But it also says that choosing

221
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:56,200
a more widespread international language

222
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,500
would have given, in its words,

223
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:01,260
concrete advantages, above all in situations

224
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:02,800
where understanding each other

225
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,580
is of fundamental importance.

226
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:06,814
Then it lists what happened.

227
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:11,020
The safety trainer testified that in practice
both Italian and English were used,

228
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:12,860
and that training was usually carried

229
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:13,760
out in English.

230
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,660
Many American passengers
testified that during

231
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:19,380
the emergency, several crew members on duty

232
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:20,760
at the muster stations

233
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:21,707
could not speak English.

234
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:25,720
And on the bridge, in the last phases,
it was proved that the helmsman

235
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:28,141
did not understand
the master's orders in English.

236
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:29,520
Twice.

237
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:33,076
There is one more finding
about language and it is administrative,

238
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,120
which is why it is easy to skip.

239
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:39,880
When the flag authority audited
the company in March 2012, it recorded

240
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,220
a formal non-conformity:

241
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:45,260
the recruitment procedure for deck
and engine personnel does not assess

242
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:46,839
the applicant's work language.

243
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,080
Nor does the procedure

244
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,554
for the service departments.

245
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:53,340
The company had chosen a language
of work, and had no step anywhere

246
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:56,168
in its hiring that checked
whether the person could speak it.

247
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:57,980
So what is a muster list worth,

248
00:08:57,980 --> 00:08:59,780
in a corridor where the person holding

249
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:01,520
it and the person reading it

250
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:02,625
do not share a language?

251
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:04,538
It is worth something.

252
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,657
Just not what the paperwork says.

253
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:08,596
That is the pattern here.

254
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,227
Nothing is absent.

255
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:12,635
Everything is thinner than it looks.

256
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:14,486
There was a language of work.

257
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,945
Nobody tested for it.

258
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:17,783
There was a muster list.

259
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,082
Some assignments were inconsistent.

260
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,141
There were muster stations,

261
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:23,721
big ones, correctly placed.

262
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:26,478
Most passengers had never walked to them.

263
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,361
There was a drill schedule.

264
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:31,459
The master had written to say
the drills were getting worse.

265
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,642
Every one of those exists on paper.

266
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,360
Not one of them had ever

267
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:38,011
been pulled on hard enough
to find out what it would hold.

268
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,380
The investigators also went through the crew

269
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:43,640
certification, the muster
list and the familiarisation

270
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,800
training, and found inconsistencies

271
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,320
in the assignment of duties

272
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,425
to some crew members.

273
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:50,560
A muster list is the document

274
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,960
that says who does what

275
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:52,860
in an emergency.

276
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,900
Which crew member takes which station.

277
00:09:58,160 --> 00:09:59,060
Which boat.

278
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:00,420
Which stairwell.

279
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:01,800
It is the whole plan,

280
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,380
on paper, in advance.

281
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,508
And it only works one way.

282
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:07,456
Somebody has to start it.

283
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:09,715
If the assignments are inconsistent,

284
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:10,790
then on the night,

285
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:12,920
two people think somebody else has the job.

286
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:15,320
And the report records the consequence

287
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,478
of no orders arriving:

288
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:18,320
the lack of direct orders

289
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,040
from the bridge left the initiative

290
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:22,720
to individuals,
and the different backgrounds

291
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:25,200
and basic training among the crew

292
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,360
may have played a part in how

293
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:27,728
the emergency was handled.

294
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:29,393
Read that carefully.

295
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:30,820
It is not saying

296
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,083
the crew were untrained.

297
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:37,000
It is saying that when nothing comes down
from the bridge, a thousand people fall back

298
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,587
on their own judgement -

299
00:10:39,588 --> 00:10:42,400
and a thousand separate judgements
is not an evacuation plan.

300
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:44,320
And someone had said so,

301
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:46,057
in writing, three months earlier.

302
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:47,754
On the fifteenth of October,

303
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:50,840
2011, this ship held an abandon-ship drill.

304
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:53,540
Afterwards, the master warned the company

305
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:55,780
that his crew's performance was decreasing,

306
00:10:55,810 --> 00:10:58,080
and that the drill
had shown critical findings.

307
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:01,480
The safety trainer, when he
joined, found the same thing

308
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,901
from a different direction:

309
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:05,020
the crew's training was unaligned,

310
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:06,960
and there was no evidence on board

311
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:10,327
of the training the company's own
safety-management procedure required.

312
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:11,958
He told his superiors.

313
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:16,348
The master told him the company had asked
the ship's management to improve the programme.

314
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:17,740
So the warning existed,

315
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:18,840
it came from the top

316
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,180
of the ship, and it went

317
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,080
to the shore.

318
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:24,848
Now the other half of the training
question, which is about the bridge rather

319
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:25,660
than the decks.

320
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,080
There is a course called

321
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:28,860
Bridge Resource Management.

322
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,380
Its entire subject is the problem

323
00:11:31,380 --> 00:11:34,000
the investigators
would later describe on page

324
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,880
eleven of their report - how

325
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,740
a bridge team is supposed to speak

326
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:39,840
up, challenge, and cross-check

327
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:41,218
the person in command.

328
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:42,960
The master of this ship

329
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,080
had never attended it.

330
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:45,611
Not the junior version,

331
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:48,640
not the senior version,
not the one for staff masters.

332
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,914
That is not a rule he broke.

333
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:53,260
He held the passenger-ship certificate

334
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:56,340
the regulations required, obtained in 2008,

335
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,620
and he had nearly seventeen years

336
00:11:58,620 --> 00:11:59,988
of sea service behind him.

337
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,380
The course simply was not mandatory.

338
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:07,040
Several of his officers had taken
it - a staff master in 2010,

339
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,320
and the chief mate,

340
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:11,100
the safety officer, a second officer

341
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,420
and two third officers during 2011,

342
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:16,066
at the group's training centre in Amsterdam.

343
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:17,960
The people trained to challenge

344
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:18,960
were on the bridge.

345
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:22,676
The person they would have been challenging
had not taken the course.

346
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:26,148
From the first of September 2012 -

347
00:12:26,149 --> 00:12:28,435
eight months after this night -

348
00:12:28,436 --> 00:12:32,467
the parent corporation made that course
mandatory, along with electronic chart training,

349
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:34,154
ship handling and stability.

350
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,580
The master and the staff master

351
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:37,738
have to attend all of them.

352
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,500
Here is the clock.

353
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:42,540
Every time in it comes

354
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:43,803
off the ship's own recorder.

355
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:45,860
Nine forty-five and seven

356
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:47,045
seconds: the contact.

357
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:50,920
At five to ten - ten minutes
after the contact - compartments four,

358
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:52,920
five, six and seven

359
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,341
are ascertained as flooded.

360
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,509
No distress message has been sent.

361
00:12:57,060 --> 00:12:58,481
No securite message either.

362
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:02,060
At thirty-four seconds
past nine fifty-seven,

363
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:05,600
the master informs the company's designated

364
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:08,790
person ashore, who leaves for the company
building to form a crisis team.

365
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,346
So the shore knows something.

366
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:12,280
Which shore, and what they were told,

367
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,340
is the whole

368
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:14,761
of the next twenty minutes.

369
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,300
At seven minutes past ten the rescue

370
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,980
organisation at Civitavecchia

371
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:19,940
contacts the ship.

372
00:13:20,660 --> 00:13:22,502
The ship tells them about the black

373
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:24,120
out, and that it is managing

374
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,477
to solve the failure.

375
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:27,093
Only the black out.

376
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:29,220
What does a rescue centre do with that?

377
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:30,673
It does what it did.

378
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:34,140
It notes a ship with an electrical
fault, off an island,

379
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:35,740
in calm weather, and it waits.

380
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:39,927
The investigators put a phrase
in their own table against that line:

381
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:42,260
very serious scenario is held back.

382
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,700
At eleven minutes past ten the ship

383
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:46,384
is adrift towards the coastline.

384
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:48,181
At twelve minutes past ten,

385
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:52,740
the public address makes its first announcement
to the passengers. It tells them to go

386
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:53,640
to the lounges.

387
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,343
Not the muster stations.

388
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,000
The lounges.

389
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:59,600
And the report records
what actually happened

390
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,920
next, which is the strangest line

391
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:02,820
in the document:

392
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:07,900
crew and passengers moved towards the muster
stations by themselves. Without an order.

393
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,720
Several thousand people, most

394
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:11,825
of whom had only watched a video,

395
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:14,812
worked out on their own where
they were supposed to be.

396
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,620
Ten past ten, near enough:

397
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:18,920
the maritime rescue coordination centre

398
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,220
at Livorno is contacted.

399
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,855
Twenty-nine minutes after the rocks.

400
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,666
At fourteen minutes past ten,

401
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:27,481
Livorno finds the ship
on its own tracking system.

402
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:30,820
The ship tells the rescue centre
that it has had a blackout

403
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:32,136
for about twenty minutes.

404
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,475
And makes no request for assistance.

405
00:14:34,890 --> 00:14:36,140
Stay with that one.

406
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:38,800
A shore station with helicopters and patrol

407
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,100
boats has a cruise ship

408
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:41,520
on the screen,

409
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:42,420
has it on the radio,

410
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:43,500
and is told:

411
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:45,380
we have had a power failure.

412
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:46,320
Not:

413
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:47,500
we have struck rocks.

414
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:48,460
Not:

415
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:49,620
we are taking water.

416
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:50,640
Not:

417
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:53,020
we have four thousand people on board

418
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:54,860
and I need everything you have.

419
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:57,680
At twenty-five minutes and fifteen seconds

420
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,840
past ten, contacted again,

421
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:01,860
the master tells Livorno there

422
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,960
is a hull breach on the left
side causing a gradual heel.

423
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:07,965
That is forty minutes after the contact,

424
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:09,340
and it is the first time

425
00:15:09,340 --> 00:15:11,024
the shore hears the word breach.

426
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:13,380
At twenty-two minutes past ten the ship

427
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:14,980
asks for the help of two tugs.

428
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:19,440
Four minutes later, the chief mate tells
the rescue authority, for the first time,

429
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,800
that there is a breach

430
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,379
and that the ship is flooding.

431
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,320
The Body's comment on that line

432
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,060
in its own table is the harshest

433
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:27,271
sentence in the report,

434
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:29,100
and it is aimed at the delay

435
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,700
rather than at any person:

436
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,560
this was an evident and very serious

437
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,920
untruth, because the breach had been known

438
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:38,913
since twenty-three seconds
past nine forty-nine.

439
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:41,365
Known on board for thirty-seven minutes.

440
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:46,117
Told to the shore at twenty-six minutes
past ten. Why would anybody hold that back?

441
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:47,880
The report does not say,

442
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,669
and this programme will not guess.

443
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,420
But it is worth knowing what

444
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:52,320
the word costs.

445
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,010
Declaring distress is not a phone call.

446
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,140
It is a legal act.

447
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:58,515
It hands the situation to the shore.

448
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:00,740
It launches helicopters, patrol boats,

449
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:04,540
tugs, and other ships pulled
off their routes. It becomes an incident

450
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:05,720
with a file attached.

451
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:07,380
So there is a pull,

452
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:09,300
in the first minutes of anything,

453
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:12,300
towards finding out a bit
more before you say it.

454
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:13,974
Towards solving it yourself.

455
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,440
That pull is not unique to ships.

456
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,760
It is in every building

457
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,260
that has ever had an alarm somebody

458
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,260
hesitated to break.

459
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:23,637
Here it lasted fifty-one minutes.

460
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:25,920
At half past ten the flooding reaches

461
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:28,040
Deck Zero, the watertight deck.

462
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,781
And passengers begin boarding
the lifeboats by themselves.

463
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:34,580
At twenty-six seconds past ten thirty-three,

464
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:36,422
the general emergency is announced.

465
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:38,580
Forty-eight minutes after the contact.

466
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:42,820
Three minutes after that comes something
that sounds like an order to abandon ship.

467
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,400
It is not one.

468
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:46,614
The words were never spoken.

469
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:50,280
What the announcement actually said
was to reach the muster stations calmly

470
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,122
and follow the crew's instructions.

471
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:55,200
At thirty-six minutes
and thirty-four seconds

472
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:57,534
past ten, Livorno calls again.

473
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:59,991
The bridge says the heeling is increasing.

474
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,380
And only then, after the rescue centre

475
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:04,660
presses, does the ship declare

476
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:06,180
that it is in distress.

477
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,047
Fifty-one minutes.

478
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,500
In that same call the bridge gives

479
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:13,952
the number of people on board
as three thousand two hundred

480
00:17:13,953 --> 00:17:17,137
and eight passengers. The true
figure was three thousand two

481
00:17:17,138 --> 00:17:18,001
hundred and six.

482
00:17:18,002 --> 00:17:20,560
And it was different again
from the figure the ship had given

483
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,420
on departure from Civitavecchia,

484
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,713
which was three thousand two

485
00:17:24,719 --> 00:17:25,750
hundred and sixteen.

486
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:27,569
Three numbers for the same people.

487
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:29,460
On the night that a shore station

488
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:30,760
needs to know how many

489
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,660
to look for.

490
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:34,360
At fifty-four minutes and ten seconds past

491
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,220
ten, the abandon ship is ordered.

492
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:39,260
Sixty-nine minutes
after the hull struck the rock.

493
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:41,660
And the finding attached to that order

494
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,580
is the one this programme exists

495
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:44,791
to put in front of you.

496
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:48,040
It was not preceded by an effective
general emergency alarm.

497
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:50,900
Several passengers testified that they never

498
00:17:50,900 --> 00:17:53,268
caught the signal,
or the voice announcement.

499
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,642
There is a sound designed for this.

500
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:58,200
Seven short blasts and one long one,

501
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,360
on a system that reaches every space

502
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:02,460
on the ship, which every passenger

503
00:18:02,460 --> 00:18:04,039
is told about in the briefing,

504
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:05,628
and which means one thing:

505
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:07,180
go to your station now.

506
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:09,080
The investigators' finding

507
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:11,027
is that it was not effectively given.

508
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:13,060
So the order to abandon a ship

509
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:15,460
reached several thousand
people who had never

510
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:16,760
been told, by the ship,

511
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:18,140
that anything was wrong.

512
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:20,820
And the ship's own paperwork said exactly

513
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:22,346
how it should have been done.

514
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:25,280
The muster list specifies
it in capital letters:

515
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:28,800
the order of the master,
through the public address of the ship,

516
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:31,900
followed by a continuous double tone sound,

517
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,500
or by the alarm bells,

518
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:35,560
until the ship evacuation is completed.

519
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:37,780
An order, and then a sound

520
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:39,020
that does not stop

521
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:39,920
until everyone is off.

522
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:44,361
What happened instead was an announcement
in English, made by the second master, once.

523
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,480
Meanwhile, ashore,
the company was assembling.

524
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:51,227
The designated person
had been told at nine fifty-seven.

525
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,920
At twenty-one minutes past ten he telephoned

526
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,080
a manager, believing him

527
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,817
to be the crisis manager on duty.

528
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,846
The manager said that he was.

529
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,531
Under the company's own written procedure,

530
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:03,140
the crisis manager on duty

531
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:05,146
was a different person -

532
00:19:05,147 --> 00:19:07,515
and that person
was not immediately informed.

533
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,260
The crisis committee was formed

534
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:10,207
at eleven o'clock.

535
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,935
Seventy-five minutes after the rock.

536
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:14,800
The first lifeboats are lowered

537
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:15,700
a minute later.

538
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,227
By ten past eleven

539
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:21,430
they are on the shore with the first
passengers. The crew, including the master,

540
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:26,140
leave the bridge at about twenty past eleven.
One officer stays behind to coordinate

541
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,040
the abandon ship.

542
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:29,760
By about midnight the heel is forty degrees.

543
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:32,520
At thirty-four minutes
past midnight a rescue

544
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:34,640
unit reports the ship listed at ninety

545
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:37,480
degrees, about fifty people still unable

546
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,380
to get off -

547
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:40,600
and that the master is not on the ship.

548
00:19:41,070 --> 00:19:43,420
Eight minutes later,
Livorno reaches the master,

549
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:45,000
who says there seem

550
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,188
to be about a hundred
passengers still aboard.

551
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:49,140
The rescue centre strongly urges him

552
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,160
to go back on board,

553
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,800
with the other officers,

554
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:54,080
and coordinate
the disembarkation of the people

555
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:54,980
who are left.

556
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:57,760
At fifty-three minutes past
midnight the evacuation

557
00:19:57,760 --> 00:19:59,000
of those still on the ship

558
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,460
begins, by helicopter.

559
00:20:01,380 --> 00:20:02,696
Twenty-five patrol boats.

560
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:04,220
Fourteen vessels.

561
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,740
Four tugs.

562
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,147
Eight helicopters.

563
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:08,773
All of that arrived.

564
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:11,260
Most of it arrived after the ship

565
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:16,880
had already been on the rocks
for over an hour. Now the physics,

566
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:17,920
because it is the only part

567
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:20,200
of this night that behaved
exactly as designed.

568
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:23,020
A large ship is divided into watertight

569
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:25,320
compartments, and the rule she is built

570
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:26,840
to is that she must survive

571
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:28,524
a given number of them flooding.

572
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:30,260
Beyond that number, no ship

573
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:32,155
of this kind can be made unsinkable.

574
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,811
The investigative body states it directly:

575
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:36,900
no measure is sufficient to render

576
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:39,360
the ship unsinkable when more than two

577
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:41,834
contiguous watertight
compartments are flooded.

578
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:44,431
The rock opened compartments five and six.

579
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:47,240
Two contiguous compartments,
violently flooded

580
00:20:47,241 --> 00:20:49,480
- compartment five filled completely

581
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,585
in a very short time.

582
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,560
So the ship was going to end

583
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:53,460
up on her side.

584
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:55,500
That was decided at the moment

585
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:57,700
of contact and nothing on board

586
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:58,620
could have changed it.

587
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:01,240
Which raises the only question that matters

588
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,766
about the rest of that night.

589
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:03,720
If the ship

590
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:05,036
could not be saved, what could?

591
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:08,260
The answer is the people,
and the answer is arithmetic.

592
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:11,296
A ship going over is not a ship going down.

593
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:13,359
It leans, and it leans slowly.

594
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:16,240
At thirteen degrees you
can still walk, badly.

595
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:19,870
At thirty the decks are ramps. At forty,

596
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:21,953
which is where she was around midnight,

597
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,360
walking is climbing.

598
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:25,450
At eighty, where she ended,

599
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,060
the corridors are shafts.

600
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:31,480
Everything had to happen in the early
part of that scale. But here is the thing

601
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:33,780
about a ship that is going over rather

602
00:21:33,781 --> 00:21:34,529
than going down.

603
00:21:34,530 --> 00:21:35,500
It takes time.

604
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,453
The heel is gradual.

605
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:40,865
The master describes it that way
himself to the rescue centre,

606
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:42,280
forty minutes in.

607
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,760
And that gradual heel is the resource.

608
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:47,540
It is the only resource anybody

609
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:49,300
had that night, and there was more

610
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:50,511
of it than anyone used.

611
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:52,940
Which is exactly what the investigators

612
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:54,080
went and calculated.

613
00:21:54,740 --> 00:21:56,529
They ran the alternative timeline.

614
00:21:57,200 --> 00:22:01,141
Suppose the general emergency signal
had been given at thirty-nine minutes past ten

615
00:22:01,171 --> 00:22:02,520
- the point at which the ship

616
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:03,760
grounded a second time,

617
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:06,240
and the first rescue vessel reached her.

618
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:10,838
Suppose the passengers had been gathered
and ready at the boats, waiting for the order.

619
00:22:11,120 --> 00:22:13,180
On that timeline the abandon ship

620
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:17,180
would have followed thirty-six minutes
after the signal - which the investigators say

621
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:19,320
is adequate to gather everybody into muster

622
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:22,320
stations they describe
as capacious and suitable.

623
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:27,193
Passengers would have started leaving the ship
while she had thirteen degrees of heel.

624
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:31,080
And thirty-three minutes after that,
when the ship reached thirty degrees,

625
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:34,260
at twelve minutes past eleven - all

626
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:36,049
of them could have reached safety.

627
00:22:36,340 --> 00:22:37,551
From the same position.

628
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:39,941
With the ship already stopped.

629
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:41,987
Where thirty-two people instead died.

630
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:44,460
That is not a campaigner's claim.

631
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:46,922
That is the official investigation,

632
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:49,120
writing down in its own report

633
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:51,060
that everybody could have got off.

634
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:53,773
And it names how those thirty-two died:

635
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:56,200
most were trapped, and the others

636
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,516
were thrown into the sea.

637
00:22:57,740 --> 00:22:59,679
Thirty people were found.

638
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:02,040
Two were never found - one passenger,

639
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:03,340
one crew member.

640
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,600
Twenty-six passengers and four crew

641
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:06,916
are recorded as deceased.

642
00:23:07,500 --> 00:23:08,400
The last was found

643
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,979
on the twenty-second of March.

644
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,820
A hundred and fifty-seven

645
00:23:12,821 --> 00:23:15,821
passengers claimed injuries. Two more
findings, and they belong together

646
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:18,160
because they are the same failure seen

647
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:19,060
from both ends.

648
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:21,980
Below decks, the engine
and electrical departments

649
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:24,243
worked the emergency from the first minute.

650
00:23:24,580 --> 00:23:26,320
Under the chief engineer they fed

651
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:27,583
the bridge a continuous,

652
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:29,740
detailed, systematically updated picture

653
00:23:29,740 --> 00:23:31,940
of the flooding, the propulsion

654
00:23:31,940 --> 00:23:33,260
and the emergency power.

655
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:35,760
The chief engineer spoke to the master

656
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:37,023
directly, several times.

657
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:40,640
They went into flooded compartments
to try to restore vital equipment,

658
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,580
at serious risk to themselves,

659
00:23:42,580 --> 00:23:43,940
and it did not work.

660
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:48,060
And they stayed on the bulkhead deck
after the water reached it - knowing

661
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:49,980
the ship was lost - and left

662
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:51,300
only when the bridge cleared

663
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:52,200
them to go.

664
00:23:52,620 --> 00:23:54,400
That is the information arriving.

665
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:56,300
Now what was leaving.

666
00:23:57,220 --> 00:23:59,040
Some crew members, meeting passengers

667
00:23:59,040 --> 00:24:01,100
in the corridors, told them to go

668
00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:02,260
back to their cabins.

669
00:24:02,740 --> 00:24:04,833
That it was only a black out.

670
00:24:04,940 --> 00:24:06,677
That it would be sorted out soon.

671
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:08,506
They were not inventing that.

672
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:10,340
It is what the ship had told

673
00:24:10,340 --> 00:24:11,708
the rescue services twice.

674
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:16,240
Passengers were not gathered
from their cabins, as the procedure requires.

675
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:20,200
And the investigators
offer one piece of proof

676
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:22,140
for that which does not need
any interpretation at all.

677
00:24:22,700 --> 00:24:25,040
Two passengers were found alive on deck

678
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:26,420
eight, three days later.

679
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:30,620
Deck eight has no lounges
and no public rooms. It is cabins.

680
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:33,380
The passengers also testified to something

681
00:24:33,380 --> 00:24:34,700
that explains why a cabin

682
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:36,068
was the worst place to be.

683
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:38,800
The public spaces stayed lit throughout

684
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:40,168
by the emergency lighting.

685
00:24:40,800 --> 00:24:42,484
The cabins were completely dark.

686
00:24:43,060 --> 00:24:47,460
People found their lifejackets in the wardrobe
by the light of a torch, or a mobile phone.

687
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:48,780
And one last

688
00:24:48,780 --> 00:24:50,200
absence, recorded flatly.

689
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:52,011
Nobody called the roll.

690
00:24:52,420 --> 00:24:53,473
Nobody attempted to.

691
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:57,460
Nobody counted the passengers as they
boarded the lifeboats and the rafts.

692
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:59,780
Not one of the several thousand people

693
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:00,640
who left that ship

694
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,851
was counted leaving it.

695
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:03,600
The Body explains why,

696
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:05,863
and its explanation is not about character.

697
00:25:06,560 --> 00:25:10,140
The lack of orders in accordance
with the muster list disoriented the crew

698
00:25:10,140 --> 00:25:13,820
who had been assigned by that same
muster list. They had been given jobs

699
00:25:13,820 --> 00:25:15,560
by a document, and then never

700
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:16,460
told to start.

701
00:25:16,860 --> 00:25:18,580
So what does the report conclude,

702
00:25:18,580 --> 00:25:19,940
at the top, in one line?

703
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:25,327
That the human element is the root
cause of the Costa Concordia casualty -

704
00:25:25,328 --> 00:25:28,140
in the action that caused
the contact, and in the management

705
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:29,614
of the emergency afterwards.

706
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:32,040
That sentence is going to be read,

707
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:33,800
by most people who read it,

708
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:34,980
as being about one man

709
00:25:34,980 --> 00:25:35,880
on a bridge.

710
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,760
An honest film has to say what

711
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:39,286
else is in the same document.

712
00:25:39,460 --> 00:25:40,460
On the bridge team,

713
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:42,063
the investigators write:

714
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:45,460
nobody seemed to have urged
the master to accelerate the turn,

715
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:46,740
or to give warning

716
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:47,898
of the looming danger.

717
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:52,160
And they say the accident may lead
to a wider discussion about the adequacy

718
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:53,820
of bridge teams - how

719
00:25:53,820 --> 00:25:55,820
they are organised, and what the people

720
00:25:55,820 --> 00:25:57,609
standing on them are actually for.

721
00:25:58,320 --> 00:25:59,660
That is not one man.

722
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:01,260
That is a room.

723
00:26:01,720 --> 00:26:02,620
On the alarm:

724
00:26:03,100 --> 00:26:05,400
the general emergency
alarm was not activated

725
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:07,080
immediately after the impact,

726
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:09,800
and that delayed
the management of everything

727
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:11,740
that came after it - the flooding,

728
00:26:11,740 --> 00:26:13,380
and the abandon ship process.

729
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:15,600
That is not one man either.

730
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:20,396
That is a procedure that did not start.
And underneath all of it:

731
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:22,760
nearly two thousand people who had never

732
00:26:22,760 --> 00:26:24,660
walked to a muster station,

733
00:26:24,660 --> 00:26:28,822
because the operation they had bought
a ticket from showed them a video instead.

734
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,895
The human element is the root cause.

735
00:26:31,560 --> 00:26:33,080
It is just not one human.

736
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:36,080
Go back to the floor.

737
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:37,620
It is level.

738
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,660
It is carpeted, and warm,

739
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:44,160
and there are several thousand people standing
on it who have no reason to look down.

740
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:46,220
That is what a ship feels like

741
00:26:46,220 --> 00:26:47,641
when everything is correct.

742
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:49,256
It feels like a building.

743
00:26:49,960 --> 00:26:52,860
The rock took the compartments
and the ship was always going

744
00:26:52,860 --> 00:26:53,760
to lie down.

745
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,480
The blackout took the rudder

746
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:57,164
and the pumps in ninety seconds.

747
00:26:57,560 --> 00:27:01,760
Neither of those could be undone by anybody
on board. What was left was time,

748
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:02,920
and there was more

749
00:27:02,920 --> 00:27:04,394
of it than the night needed.

750
00:27:04,860 --> 00:27:06,544
Sixty-nine minutes to the order.

751
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:08,260
Another eighteen before the heel

752
00:27:08,260 --> 00:27:09,471
reached thirty degrees.

753
00:27:10,140 --> 00:27:11,040
Thirteen degrees.

754
00:27:11,580 --> 00:27:12,480
Thirty.

755
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:13,780
Forty.

756
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:14,940
Eighty.

757
00:27:15,420 --> 00:27:18,800
Somewhere in the middle of that,
the investigators say, every person aboard

758
00:27:18,800 --> 00:27:21,400
could have been standing
on a rock in the Tyrrhenian Sea,

759
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:23,579
cold and frightened and alive.

760
00:27:24,340 --> 00:27:25,393
They needed a sound.

761
00:27:25,780 --> 00:27:26,720
Given once.

762
00:27:27,500 --> 00:27:28,910
In the first minutes.

763
00:27:28,940 --> 00:27:31,100
On a system that reaches every room.

764
00:27:31,620 --> 00:27:33,020
And a walk that most of them

765
00:27:33,020 --> 00:27:33,920
had never taken.

766
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:36,580
Tonight, on ships all over the world,

767
00:27:36,940 --> 00:27:38,880
several thousand people at a time put

768
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:40,420
on an orange jacket and stand

769
00:27:40,420 --> 00:27:41,946
in a marked square on a deck,

770
00:27:42,180 --> 00:27:43,720
feeling faintly silly,

771
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:44,900
while somebody counts them.

772
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:47,006
That is the whole difference.
